---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DataControls from '@/components/DataControls.tsx';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy - Skillsets.cc">
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <header class="mb-8 border-b border-border-ink pb-6">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-medium font-serif text-text-ink">Privacy</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-lg font-serif text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium font-serif text-text-ink mb-3">What we collect</h2>
        <p>When you log in with GitHub, we receive your GitHub user ID, login name, and avatar URL. If you star a skillset, we store the skillset ID in a list keyed to your user ID.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium font-serif text-text-ink mb-3">How we use it</h2>
        <p>Your login name is used to display your authentication status. Your starred skillset list powers the star feature — that's it.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium font-serif text-text-ink mb-3">Cookies</h2>
        <p>We set a single <code class="text-accent font-mono text-base">session</code> cookie — httpOnly, secure, SameSite=Lax, 7-day expiry. It contains a JWT with your GitHub ID, login, and avatar URL. No tracking cookies, no analytics cookies.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium font-serif text-text-ink mb-3">Data retention</h2>
        <p>Your starred skillsets persist until you delete your account. Rate limit entries and session revocation records auto-expire. Download counts are keyed by IP address, not user ID.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium font-serif text-text-ink mb-3">Your rights</h2>
        <p>You can view, export, and delete your data using the controls below (visible when logged in). Exported data is returned as JSON per GDPR Article 20. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium font-serif text-text-ink mb-3">Contributors</h2>
        <p>Skillset submissions are public git history. To request removal of a published skillset, open an issue or email us. We'll remove the listing from the registry. Git history retention is GitHub's responsibility.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium font-serif text-text-ink mb-3">GitHub authorization</h2>
        <p>Deleting your account on skillsets.cc removes your data from our systems. The OAuth app authorization on your GitHub account persists — revoke it at Settings &gt; Applications &gt; Authorized OAuth Apps.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium font-serif text-text-ink mb-3">Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions or requests: <a href="mailto:hello@skillsets.cc" class="text-accent hover:underline">hello@skillsets.cc</a></p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <DataControls client:load />
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
